  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Same-origin request path",
      "items": [
        "CloudFront single origin: browser /api/* proxies straight to the shared HTTP API — no CORS, first-party cookies",
        "One foodo-jwt REQUEST authorizer verifies the HS256 session cookie or Bearer token; denials return 403 at the gateway",
        "Role checks (isSeller / isRider / isAdmin) stay inside each service"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Event-driven core",
      "items": [
        "Services publish domain events to one SNS topic; each service owns its inbound queue, DLQ and filter policy",
        "SQS work queues (payment, order) carry cross-service jobs; redrive to DLQ after 3 failed receives",
        "Restaurant and rider services each own an inbound queue: rider.* and payment.intent.created return to the restaurant service, order.cancelled · delivered · rejected to the rider service",
        "Realtime's eventConsumer subscribes to the topic and broadcasts every event to rooms via the WebSocket Management API"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "State + provisioned for later",
      "items": [
        "Eight shared DynamoDB tables (pk/sk + GSIs): users, restaurants, menu, carts, orders, addresses, payments and the riders table",
        "TTL sweeps unpaid orders, refresh tokens and webhook dedupe rows",
        "Realtime owns its own ephemeral connections table (TTL'd)",
        "Cognito pool and S3 uploads bucket are provisioned for the issuer/upload migration — idle today"
      ]
    }
  ]
